WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:06.749
Hey, David, between the legal challenges and
the not conceding and claiming he won and

00:00:06.749 --> 00:00:12.259
lawsuits and electoral ideas, what is Donald
Trump's actual end game here?

00:00:12.259 --> 00:00:15.599
Does he think he will be inaugurated to a
second term?

00:00:15.599 --> 00:00:16.810
I think the answer is no.

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:21.220
I think at this point, Donald Trump knows
he's not getting a second term.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:27.860
And for me, you know, there's been a lot of
focus about Trump's lawsuits having the goal

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:34.130
of throwing out so-called illegal votes or
getting a recount that changes the results.

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:40.120
I think if we want to for a second believe
that there's some bigger strategy here and

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:44.059
there may not be, but let's imagine there
is some bigger strategy.

00:00:44.059 --> 00:00:49.920
The more likely strategy, the more likely
to be effective strategy here would be that

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:56.949
Donald Trump is merely trying to get a court
to prevent a state from certifying its election.

00:00:56.949 --> 00:01:03.800
If you can prevent state legislatures from
certifying the election results, you then

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:08.120
can create a situation where state legislators
get to pick electors.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:10.960
This is part of three USC Section two.

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:15.350
Now, this is different than what I talked
about in an earlier segment where I said you're

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:18.460
not going to get enough faithless electors.

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:22.930
You're not going to get willy nilly states
to just send different electors.

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:27.740
But there's this scenario where if you can
actually delay certification, state legislatures

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:30.140
get to appoint electors.

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:35.900
And for me, if there is a strategy and I don't
know that there is these people have shown

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:37.790
themselves to be incompetent.

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:40.920
Everything they're filing is being thrown
out.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:45.680
If there were a strategy, it would be that
I still think it's unlikely because I don't

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:52.760
know that I see a court staying, in other
words, pausing certification by any state

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:59.190
in such a way that it will go further than
roughly December 14th, which is when that

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:02.150
electoral vote is set to happen.

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:03.660
I don't see that happening.

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:08.080
Courts have been moving very quickly, oftentimes
will have a lawsuit and then two days later,

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:09.420
the court throws it out.

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:13.310
Courts understand the time sensitivity of
this.

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:18.340
So given that, I don't think Trump really
believes he has a shot at overturning the

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:22.969
election results, it seems to me that this
is either just Donald Trump's delusional,

00:02:22.969 --> 00:02:27.770
narcissistic ego who can't admit that he lost,
even if he sort of knows he knows he's going

00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:28.770
to be pushed out.

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:29.770
He simply can't admit it.

00:02:29.770 --> 00:02:30.819
And he says, file every lawsuit.

00:02:30.819 --> 00:02:32.260
You can do everything you can.

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:38.680
It might simply be that it could be Donald
Trump planning to undermine Joe Biden not

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:41.239
only now, but through his presidency.

00:02:41.239 --> 00:02:42.239
And this is just part of it.

00:02:42.239 --> 00:02:47.620
Never admitting that he actually lost it could
be that Donald Trump is trying to hand Joe

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:53.439
Biden the most chaotic possible situation
he can on January 20th.

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:57.819
And continuing to further these lawsuits is
part of that.

00:02:57.819 --> 00:03:02.189
And it could be that Donald Trump is simply
trying to smoothly transition right into some

00:03:02.189 --> 00:03:05.220
kind of media project, which has been hypothesized
by many.

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:10.680
Trump wants to do some kind of challenger
to Fox News, some kind of outfoxing Fox News

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:12.840
with some kind of Trump news network.

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:18.870
All of these things I find myself saying,
OK, we'll deal with that one when we come

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:23.620
to it, if we do after Donald Trump has left
office on January 20th.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:26.470
But I don't see any end game beyond that.

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:30.150
And if you really think Donald Trump is doing
this because he thinks he's going to get a

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:32.360
second term, I want to hear from you.

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:33.959
I just don't see it.

00:03:33.959 --> 00:03:38.870
We have a great bonus show for you today,
after which we will be off Thursday and Friday

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:40.299
for Thanksgiving.

00:03:40.299 --> 00:03:43.659
I will be back with you on Monday, Monday.

00:03:43.659 --> 00:03:45.040
Have a good holiday.

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:47.110
If you're celebrating, be safe.

00:03:47.110 --> 00:03:48.110
Very important.

00:03:48.110 --> 00:03:48.112
Be safe.

